    "result_text": "Done. There is only one test class in the suite (`AcceptanceTest`), and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change: the create audit line now also logs `membershipLevel` and `membershipNumber`, keeping every field it already logged.\n\nI made a single, focused edit to `AuditOwnerCreated.service(...)`:\n- Injected the existing `OwnerMapper` bean (injected by type, exactly as `RespondWithOwnerCreated` and other functions already do).\n- Extended the audit format string with `membershipNumber={}` and passed `ownerMapper.membershipNumber(owner)`.\n\n`membershipLevel` was already present in the log line; the task's phrasing lists it alongside `membershipNumber`, so both are now guaranteed in the output.\n\nRather than duplicating the `<customerCode>-M<YY>` derivation into the audit class, I reused `OwnerMapper.membershipNumber(owner)` \u2014 the same method the response DTO uses \u2014 so the audit line and the API response can never drift apart, and the derivation logic stays in one place. Nothing else was added to the class, keeping it a single-responsibility audit step.\n\nVerified output line:\n```\nAUDIT - owner created: id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E registrationDate=2026-09-18 membershipLevel=2 membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M26\n```\n\nFull test suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
